{"timestamp": 1779383973.4501991, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 11, "data": {"caller": "player_0", "reason": "Alice reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "weapons", "victim_name": "Charlie"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779383973.450718, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 11, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779383978.863171, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I found Charlie's body in weapons just now. My route was medbay \u2192 electrical \u2192 security \u2192 weapons. The only player I saw on the way was Diana, who entered electrical from security at tick 5 while I was passing through.\n\nSince I came from security into weapons and the body was already there, whoever killed Charlie likely came from cafeteria side, or was in weapons before me. I'd like to hear where everyone else was \u2014 especially Bob, Eve, and Frank, since I can't account for any of them."}}
{"timestamp": 1779383986.3267891, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "My route was weapons \u2192 security \u2192 navigation. I started in weapons at tick 1, then moved to security where I saw Charlie, Diana, and Frank. Charlie was alive in security at tick 4 when I last saw him. Frank entered security from weapons at tick 3, and Diana came in from navigation at tick 3. After that I headed to navigation to do my task.\n\nOne thing worth noting for Alice: you said you went medbay \u2192 electrical \u2192 security \u2192 weapons, but I was in security around ticks 2-4 and I didn't see you pass through. Frank came from weapons into security at tick 3, so Frank was in weapons earlier. Charlie was still alive in security at tick 4, so whoever killed him in weapons did so after that.\n\nAlice, can you clarify exactly which ticks you were in security and weapons? And Frank \u2014 you came from weapons, were you alone there? I'd like to hear from Frank and Diana especially."}}
{"timestamp": 1779383995.871936, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "My route was navigation \u2192 security \u2192 electrical \u2192 medbay. I can confirm Bob's account \u2014 at tick 3 I was in security and saw Bob, Charlie, and Frank there. Frank did come in from weapons at tick 3. Charlie was alive at that point.\n\nAfter that I moved to electrical, where I saw Alice at tick 5. So Alice's claim of going electrical \u2192 security \u2192 weapons is contradicted \u2014 I saw her in electrical at tick 5, not coming from security. And Bob says she never passed through security either. That's a serious problem with Alice's story.\n\nAlso, Alice claimed she saw me enter electrical from security at tick 5 \u2014 but I was already in electrical, coming from security earlier, and Alice was the one in electrical at tick 5 with me. She's got the direction wrong, or she's lying about her route.\n\nFrank was in weapons before security, so he had opportunity too, but Charlie was alive in security at tick 4 per Bob. Whoever killed Charlie did it after \u2014 and Alice is the one who \"found\" the body in weapons while her route doesn't check out. I'm leaning toward Alice. Let's hear from Eve and Frank."}}
{"timestamp": 1779384036.829587, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I can confirm parts of Bob/Diana\u2019s timeline. I started cafeteria, went into weapons first \u2014 nobody dead there then \u2014 then I went down into security. I saw Bob and Charlie in security around that time, and Charlie was definitely alive. I also saw Charlie leave security toward weapons, and Bob later went toward navigation.\n\nI did pass back through weapons toward cafeteria after that, and Charlie was still alive when I saw him there, so the kill had to be after he got to weapons, not before. I didn\u2019t see Alice come through security at all, which lines up with Bob saying that too.\n\nThe biggest red flag to me is Alice\u2019s route not matching two people\u2019s accounts. If she really went electrical \u2192 security \u2192 weapons, Bob or I should\u2019ve seen her in/near security, and Diana\u2019s saying the electrical timing/direction is wrong too. I\u2019m leaning Alice unless Eve has something that clears her."}}
{"timestamp": 1779384042.8698082, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I don't have much to add from my side \u2014 I was down in storage then lower engine the whole time and didn't see anyone, so I can't directly vouch for or against anyone.\n\nBut listening to everyone else, the case against Alice is pretty strong. Bob, Diana, and Frank all independently place themselves in security around ticks 3-4 with Charlie alive, and none of them saw Alice pass through. Diana also says Alice was already in electrical at tick 5, not coming from security like Alice claimed. And Alice's description of Diana entering electrical from security contradicts Diana's own route.\n\nThree accounts that line up with each other versus one route that doesn't check out \u2014 that's enough for me. I'm voting Alice."}}
{"timestamp": 1779384053.346934, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "Wait \u2014 I already gave my speech first. Let me respond to what's been said since, because there's a serious coordination problem here.\n\nI stand by my route: medbay \u2192 electrical \u2192 security \u2192 weapons. I was in electrical at tick 5, which is exactly when Diana says she saw me there \u2014 so that part actually confirms my story, not contradicts it. The question is just direction.\n\nBut here's what's strange: Bob claims he was in security around ticks 2-4 and didn't see me, but I passed through security on my way to weapons. Frank also claims to have been in security around then. And Diana says she was in security at tick 3 and then moved to electrical, where she saw me at tick 5.\n\nIf Diana left security for electrical before tick 5, and I was in security between electrical and weapons, then Bob and Frank should have overlapped with me \u2014 unless their timelines are off, or they're coordinating a story. Three people all placing themselves in security together at the same time, all conveniently vouching for each other, is suspicious in its own right with only one Duck in the game.\n\nI am the Goose. I found the body and reported it \u2014 a Duck wouldn't self-report when they could just walk away. Please don't railroad me based on a story three players are telling in lockstep. Eve was alone in storage with no alibi either. Think carefully before voting."}}
{"timestamp": 1779384067.141706, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "To be clear on my timeline: I was in weapons at tick 1-2, moved to security where I saw Charlie alive at ticks 2, 3, and 4, then headed to navigation. Diana entered security from navigation at tick 3, and Frank entered from weapons at tick 3 \u2014 both confirmed by my own eyes, not just their words. Frank was still in security at tick 5 when I left toward navigation.\n\nAlice, here's the problem with your rebuttal: you're suggesting Diana, Frank, and I are \"coordinating\" \u2014 but I witnessed Diana and Frank's entries into security with my own eyes at tick 3, independently. That's not a story we made up together; that's three separate accounts converging on the same facts.\n\nAlso, your route claim still doesn't work. If you went electrical \u2192 security \u2192 weapons, you'd have had to pass through security after tick 4 (when I left) but before whenever the kill happened. Frank says he was still in security at tick 5 and didn't see you. And Diana places you in electrical at tick 5, which means you couldn't have been in security between electrical and weapons in any normal timeline \u2014 you'd have to have gone electrical \u2192 weapons directly, skipping security entirely, OR your route is fabricated.\n\nThe \"I self-reported so I must be innocent\" argument doesn't hold \u2014 reporting your own kill is a classic Duck move to control the narrative. I'm leaning Alice. Let's hear Eve out, but I think the evidence is pointing one direction."}}
{"timestamp": 1779384075.417841, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I'll keep this brief since I already gave my main account earlier and Bob just made the case clearly.\n\nAlice, your \"coordination\" defense doesn't hold up. Bob, Frank, and I weren't telling each other a story \u2014 Bob saw me enter security from navigation at tick 3 with his own eyes, and I saw Bob, Charlie, and Frank there independently. Three players converging on the same facts is what truth looks like, not a conspiracy.\n\nAnd to be precise about electrical: I moved from security to electrical after tick 3, and you arrived in electrical at tick 5. You did not come from security \u2014 Bob and Frank both confirm you never passed through. So your route is fabricated.\n\nEve being alone in storage is a fair point in isolation, but storage is nowhere near weapons where Charlie died. Alice \"finding\" the body in weapons with a route that three of us can disprove is far more damning.\n\nI'm voting Alice."}}
{"timestamp": 1779384095.4075599, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Yeah, my account hasn\u2019t changed.\n\nI went cafeteria \u2192 weapons \u2192 security \u2192 back through weapons \u2192 cafeteria. Early in weapons there was no body. In security I saw Bob, and Charlie was alive there. I saw Charlie leave security toward weapons, then later I passed back through weapons and saw Charlie there alive around tick 6 before I continued up toward cafeteria.\n\nThe important part is: I never saw Alice pass through security, and if her route was really electrical \u2192 security \u2192 weapons, that\u2019s exactly where she should have appeared. Bob didn\u2019t see her either, and Diana\u2019s timing puts Alice in electrical at tick 5, which makes Alice\u2019s claimed path really awkward.\n\nAlice saying \u201ca Duck wouldn\u2019t self-report\u201d doesn\u2019t clear her \u2014 self-reports happen all the time when someone wants to control the story. Given that her route is the one not matching everyone else\u2019s sightings, I\u2019m still voting Alice."}}
{"timestamp": 1779384102.3619578, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I already gave my speech earlier, but to reiterate now that we've heard everyone: Alice's route still doesn't check out. Three independent accounts \u2014 Bob, Diana, and Frank \u2014 all place each other in security at ticks 3-4 with Charlie alive, and none of them saw Alice pass through. Diana puts Alice in electrical at tick 5 arriving from a different direction than she claimed.\n\nAlice's \"you're all coordinating\" defense is weak \u2014 Bob personally witnessed Diana and Frank entering security, so it's not just everyone parroting each other. And the self-report defense doesn't clear her either; controlling the narrative is exactly why Ducks self-report.\n\nI'm voting Alice. Everyone else, please do the same \u2014 a split vote helps the Duck."}}
